fix.summary:
I checked all eight findings against the code and fixed each one. All gates pass on the final tree: Docker all (47/47 native, coverage 98.4% lines / 91.5% branches, arduino.ino 100/100, 1147 Python tests). The AVR Rev 3 build leaves 3377 B free and Rev 2 leaves 3399 B. The two protected files are unchanged (arduino.ino 31a15639…, telemetry.cpp d59aa784…). I committed nothing, flashed nothing and opened no serial port. I tested a copy of the design's Python reference with these fixes against every real move (40 end-current goldens, 42 moves from today's PWM 128/150 logs, 147 quicktest moves) and 2895 shortened real end approaches. Then I ported the fixes to C++, and the C++ matches the Python sample for sample.

F1 (confirmed): a slow-arrival switch now also needs the current at or below 90% of iRef (CAL_END_SWITCH_SLOW_IREF_PCT). The FRHL trace (clearance-FR-115750#7) is now Stuck at k=109 instead of Switch at k=104. Only one other real verdict moved: the FLKL uncurl in rodscale-knee_out fires one sample later.

F2 (confirmed; I did the design pass): this only changes moves that would otherwise end Stuck, so no existing Switch or Stop verdict changes. A curl that stalls with fewer than 12 normal-speed samples since arming (CAL_END_SHORT_NORMAL_SAMPLES), and whose last forward edge came fewer than 40 samples after arming (CAL_END_SHORT_RUN_SAMPLES), now ends Still, the plain stall. A retracting curl only gets this when its median current is at or below iRef, so a motor stalled mid-stroke stays Stuck. Uncurls are never affected. On full traces, the design rule called 51 of 2895 shortened approaches stuck; the new rule calls none, and all 40 goldens keep their verdicts. The real short ends had at most 6 normal samples and 33 samples to their last edge; the long FRKL curl at PWM 80 (27 normal samples) and the FRHL stall (7 normal samples, last edge 71 samples after arming, current above iRef) stay Stuck.

F3 (confirmed): the code still caps the knee nudge at 128. The blind-knee numbers are re-derived from today's PWM 128 logs: up to about 95 edges out, against the old claim of 58. kSpecBlindKneeNudgeMaxEdges went from 49 to 95. I removed "its hip stays curled" from SETUP.md and from the comments.

F4 (confirmed): an unarmed curl that has made 12 or more edges now uses the 1000 ms stall window instead of 500 ms. The GUI help, the glossary and SETUP.md now say that slow drives, and curls that start close to their end, find their end by stall alone. CAL_PWM_MIN is still 40.

F5 (confirmed): the manager is now 257 bytes on the heap (0x101) and each LinearActuator 82 bytes, about 763 B of heap after setup including malloc headers. That leaves about 2614 B for the stack on Rev 3 and 2636 B on Rev 2, against the compile-time figures of 3377 / 3399. Before this change it was about 2763 B. I did not make the manager static, because arduino.ino must stay byte-identical.

F6 (confirmed): a Return whose nudge showed no evidence now drives at least the nudge time plus CAL_STALL_WINDOW_MS, so a blind hip curls back for 3 s instead of 2 s.

F7: the replay fixture now holds 94 moves and 8560 samples, in three groups:
- the 40 end-current goldens;
- the 42 moves from today's logs, with the FRHL trace expected Stuck;
- 12 real end approaches started later in the same approach (11 expected Still, plus the shortened FRHL stall expected Stuck).

New detector tests cover:
- the FRHL trace;
- the short-curl replays and the PWM 128 runs by end kind;
- a retracting stall whose current swings ±30%;
- short and long synthetic curls, and the retract current guard;
- a slow curl that pauses mid-stroke.

The timeline now:
- has a per-rod taper length;
- judges presses and arrivals at the calibration PWM;
- checks ends reached within 1.2 s (they must stop within 1150 ms);
- has a new test where hips and knees start 15-200 edges from their curl end.

I updated two leg tests for F4 and F6. Each fix was reverted one at a time and at least one test failed every time (log: scratchpad\fix-mutation.log).

F8 (confirmed): the krabby_mcu docstring examples now use 128, with a new test. calibration_end_detector.h is now CRLF.

Scratch tools are in C:\Users\nickm\AppData\Local\Temp\claude\78c86551260afdf9\720ce176-f876-4a62-9959-4e2b88a4d5da\scratchpad\ced-fix (detector.py, evaluate.py, gen_fixture.py, mutate.py).
